q=dict(audit_spec_version=1,disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',question='In a stable configuration containing three voters and a nonvoter, can a verification future consume the nonvoter worker notification as the missing quorum contribution and complete successfully while no remote voter notification has contributed to that verification?',importance='Verification is a public authority check advertised for avoiding stale FSM reads. Counting a participant that cannot constrain a competing election could weaken that check. The proposed local obligation concerns verification participant eligibility, not proof of a competing election, a stale read, log divergence or overall consensus failure.',source_ids=ss,participants=['Local leader voter','Two remote voters','Configured nonvoter'],objects=['verifyFuture','followerReplication.notify','latest Configuration'],contexts=['One leader-state generation','Stable membership with three voters and one nonvoter','One independently identified verification future'],event_paths=['Public VerifyLeader -> leaderLoop -> verifyLeader -> per-worker registration -> heartbeat/replication reply -> notifyAll -> verifyFuture.vote -> leaderLoop -> future.Error'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['b-heartbeat','b-notify-replication','b-verify','b-leader-life'],fact_ids=['f-verification-notification'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b-config':'Stable membership determines worker suffrage and voter-majority threshold.','b-campaign':'A real elected-leader prefix can replace assumed leader state.','b-lease':'Voter-contact lease can terminate the leader and must remain active or be explicitly bounded in an isolated consumer comparison.','b-append':'Actual recipient can produce heartbeat success without voting eligibility.','b-replicate':'Alternative successful append path drains the same pending notifications and must be controlled or counted.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Lease counts only voters and eventually demotes an isolated leader.','Any delivered negative verification notification can cause failure before threshold completion.','Worker notification map draining and voteLock prevent repeated final notification; duplicate counting is not the current proposition.','Single-voter clusters legitimately complete from self support.','A successfully verified peer is not proven to have lost leadership merely because it cannot reach other voters at an instant.'],unknowns=['No same-execution admitted verification, supporter identities or endpoint have been measured.','An executed real election/configuration prefix is needed for a reachable-cluster conclusion; direct leader-state construction would establish only a conditional consumer result.','Transport controls must account for already in-flight ordinary append and heartbeat replies; a partition call alone does not prove that no voter notification contributes.','Broader stale-read consequence requires a distinct later-term election and observed application endpoint.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Accepted map establishes an all-peer registration loop with voter-only threshold and a notification object that drops suffrage. Newly acquired developer documentation explicitly identifies voters as VerifyLeader recipients; healthy/partial-connect tests support majority availability rather than an all-voters response requirement.')
