o=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='For a verification in an unchanged configuration with three voters including the local leader, successful quorum completion must not be obtained from local self support plus only nonvoter worker notifications. At least one distinct remote configured voter must contribute positive support to that verification before successful completion.',source_ids=ss,scope=dict(description='Participant-eligibility check of one verification future in one leader generation under fixed three-voter plus one-nonvoter membership. Compare nonvoter-only remote positive support against a permitted remote-voter control. This is a necessary-condition check, not an eventual-success or all-voters requirement.',assumptions=['Operation identity and worker suffrage are independently recorded and fixed during each comparison.','No remote voter contribution is inferred from connectivity alone: pending registrations, reply delivery and alternate successful append paths must be accounted for.','The executed artifact must declare whether authority/configuration prefix is real or supplied. Supplied state yields only a conditional local result.','Network loss/delay is non-Byzantine; replies used as positive support must come from actual implementation or be identified as a conditional substitute.'],excluded=['A later leader election or stale FSM read unless separately observed.','Configuration transitions, self removal, shutdown and disaster recovery during the comparison.','General liveness failure from an unfinished verification or tool timeout.']),pending=['Construct and execute a correlated check with nonvoter and voter control cases.'],grounding=dict(source_ids=['s-leader-loop','s-repl-ownership','s-verify-vote','s-replication','s-heartbeat','s-transfer'],expectation_ids=['s-verify-documentation','s-verify-api','s-membership-contract','s-verify-tests'],binding_ids=[b['id'] for b in bind],derivation='Developer documentation describes VerifyLeader heartbeats to voters to confirm authority, while the API promises an authority check usable to prevent stale reads. Membership declarations distinguish voting participants from nonvoters. The implementation threshold and partial-connect test clarify majority support, not unanimity. Together these support the necessary eligibility condition: a nonvoter notification cannot substitute for the remote voter needed in a three-voter verification quorum. Code asymmetry motivates the comparison but is not itself the normative source. No eventual success is required when eligible support is absent.',applicability='Applies to ordinary VerifyLeader with stable membership including nonvoters; this is an implementation authority-check contract. No requirement that a disconnected node instantly changes its local role is asserted.',unresolved=['Documentation does not define a linearization point or complete read protocol; these remain outside the local eligibility claim.','Measurement of producer identity, registration and terminal public result remains required.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Lease may terminate the old leader later, but does not qualify an earlier nonvoter contribution.','Negative support can reject verification; schedule must preserve or finitely delay this path and report its handling.','Current authority might in fact persist despite lost communication; the obligation constrains verification support rather than asserting a competing leader.']))
s=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Select notification consumption at the authority-verification boundary as the first discriminator on the accepted map. The new documentation supplies applicable expectation beyond code asymmetry. Register a narrow necessary-condition obligation before constructing its direct check.',sources=sources,question=q,obligation=o,bindings=bind,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['s-verify-documentation','s-verify-tests','s-leader-loop','s-repl-ownership','s-verify-vote'],answered='Source review aligns the lead with voter eligibility in verification, rather than treating loss of connectivity as proof of lost authority or stale reads. Majority support is sufficient in the existing partial-connect test, so the obligation does not require every voter response.',remaining=q['unknowns'],understanding='updated',rationale='The accepted notification lifecycle and context already express the relevant producer/consumer relation; no map revision is necessary to add this scoped contract. Real-producer execution with correlated supporter identities is the next discriminator. Heartbeat term and pipeline error leads remain separate frontier options.'))
